# The deploy image build context is the repo root. Keep out of it: secrets (they
# are MOUNTED at runtime, never baked in — the CA key is the whole compromise if
# it leaks), local env files, the git history, build output, and the web/node
# tree the Go image does not need.
.git
.github
secrets/
**/.env
**/.env.*
bin/
# node_modules anywhere (the web tree is nested at internal/control/api/web);
# the SPA is built fresh in the image's web stage, so a host dist is not used.
**/node_modules
internal/control/api/web/dist
lab/
docs/
*.md
